  "id": "COMPOUND:21508 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Launobine is implicated in the biological activity of SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions involving the MIP (Molecular Interaction Protein) pathway. The evidence suggests that Launobine acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which are ultimately directed toward SK-VLB. These compounds, including (5R,8R,9R,10R,13R,14R,17S)-17-[(2R)-5-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-2-methyloxolan-2-yl]-4,4,8,10,14-pentamethyl-1,2,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, are all known to target SK-VLB. This indicates that Launobine may function as a bridge in the signaling cascade, directing these compounds to SK-VLB, which could suggest a role in modulating SK-VLB activity. The consistent presence of MIP as a target of Launobine and its involvement in targeting SK-VLB implies a potential mechanism where Launobine influences the activity of these compounds, possibly through direct or indirect interactions. The evidence supports a relationship where Launobine is linked to SK-VLB via MIP, with the compounds acting as intermediates in this process.",
